# #110 camera by parity: the match camera is confirmed state (the canonical checksum holds its
# position, distance and subject boxes), so a native run equal to the headless one moves the
# camera exactly as the headless run that `bun scripts/cameraFeel.ts` measures. Archer a and
# Rifleman b spread apart, jump, cross and close in; syntax: smashcraft:docs/native-bot-session.md.
#! chat -dev quick
# Spread apart: a dashes left, b right.
60 a stick -1 0
60 b stick 1 0
62 a stick 0 0
62 b stick 0 0
# a full jumps and double jumps: the camera rises and widens.
150 a tap B 8
170 a tap B 8
# b jumps while a lands.
240 b tap B 8
# Close in: both dash toward the centre.
330 a stick 1 0
330 b stick -1 0
332 a stick 0 0
332 b stick 0 0
# View held a second: the first moment.
500 a press VIEW
570 a release VIEW
# Apart again, with jumps on both sides.
600 a stick -1 0
602 a stick 0 0
640 b tap B 8
700 a tap B 8
720 a tap B 8
800 b stick 1 0
802 b stick 0 0
900 a stick 1 0
902 a stick 0 0
# Expected, frame by frame (headless run of this script):
#! expect a 153 applied jump 1 double 0
#! expect a 170 applied jump 2 double 1
#! expect b 245 applied jump 1 double 0
#! expect b 645 applied jump 2 double 0
#! expect a 703 applied jump 3 double 0
#! expect a 720 applied jump 4 double 1
#! absent a 1-850 damage
#! absent b 1-850 damage
1000 a press VIEW
1070 a release VIEW
